    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i look at my dad and my uncle and i just see the same patterns. it's like it's all hardcoded into my dna. no matter what i do or how much therapy i try, it feels like i'm just waiting for the clock to run out. like the ending is already written and i’m just playing out the scenes.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds incredibly heavy to feel so bound by generational patterns and a sense of predestination. Recognizing these patterns is actually a powerful first step toward understanding your inheritance. Even if the foundation feels fixed, you have the agency to consciously choose which scenes you want to highlight or change within that script. Remember that your present actions are not just playing out the ending, but actively writing the next moments.",
